# MECHANISM PIN — order and duration WITHOUT numerals.
#
# The fixture is INLINE by design (see nibli-pin's module docs): the subject is the
# ENGINE's ability to reason about order, not any particular knowledge base.
#
# Why this file exists. A consuming project asked for "a primitive that expresses ORDER
# and DURATION without numerals", believing none existed — its artifact was printing an
# admission to readers that the design "never says when". No new primitive was needed:
# the committed corpus already carries `earlier`/`later` (a binary time-sequence
# ordering), `continue`/`cease` (an interval running or stopped) and `time` (a duration
# named as the interval between two events), none of which has a numeric place. What was
# missing was that this is GUARANTEED rather than incidental. These pins are that
# guarantee: they fail loudly if a refactor, a corpus regeneration, or a change to rule
# firing takes any of it away.
#
# The honest boundary is pinned too, at the bottom: an ABSOLUTE magnitude still needs a
# numeral. Ordering is qualitative; "five years" is not.

# ── ORDER ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `earlier(x1, x2)` is "x1 is earlier than x2 in time sequence" (gismu purci).
# Transitivity is NOT built in — the engine is a logic engine and the KB states its
# axioms. This is the rule a KB writes, and it must keep compiling and firing.
:accept
all $a, $b, $c: earlier($a,$b) & earlier($b,$c) -> earlier($a,$c).

earlier(Arrest, Trial).
earlier(Trial, Release).

? earlier(Arrest, Release).
# => TRUE

# Order is DIRECTIONAL: the closure must not make the relation symmetric.
? earlier(Release, Arrest).
# => FALSE

# The chain must survive more links than the default chain depth, because the rule
# bisects (a -> c via any midpoint) rather than walking one step at a time.
earlier(Release, Review).
earlier(Review, Expunge).
? earlier(Arrest, Expunge).
# => TRUE

# `later` is the converse spelling, and is INDEPENDENT: asserting one does not derive
# the other. A KB that wants both directions links them with its own rule.
? later(Release, Arrest).
# => FALSE

# ── STILL RUNNING vs ENDED ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `continue(x1, x2)` — x1 (event/state) continues over interval x2 (gismu ranji).
# `cease(x1, x2)`   — x1 ceases activity/process/state x2 (gismu sisti).
continue(Term, Custody).
cease(Parole, Custody).

? continue(Term, Custody).
# => TRUE

# "NOT YET" — the thing the ask believed was inexpressible because `~past P` is refused.
# Negation-as-failure over an ordinary relation says it directly, no tense involved.
? ~cease(Term, Custody).
# => TRUE

? ~cease(Parole, Custody).
# => FALSE

# And a rule may READ that, which is the part that makes it usable in a constitution.
:accept
all $e: continue($e, Custody) & ~cease($e, Custody) -> occurrence($e).

? occurrence(Term).
# => TRUE

? occurrence(Parole).
# => FALSE

# ── DURATION AS A NAMED INTERVAL ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# `time(x1, x2, x3)` — x1 is the interval FROM x2 TO x3 (gismu temci). Arity 3, no
# numeric place: a duration is named by its endpoints, never measured.
:accept
time(Sentence, Trial, Release).

? time(Sentence, Trial, Release).
# => TRUE

# The endpoints are ordered, so a duration inherits the ordering of what bounds it.
? earlier(Trial, Release).
# => TRUE

# ── A CONTRADICTORY ORDER IS DETECTABLE ──────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing in the engine enforces asymmetry — `earlier` is an ordinary relation. A KB
# that needs the guarantee derives it, the same way `utopia.nibli` derives `false`.
:accept
all $a, $b: earlier($a,$b) & earlier($b,$a) -> broken($a).

earlier(Muddle, Tangle).
earlier(Tangle, Muddle).

? broken(Muddle).
# => TRUE

# The consistent chain above must NOT be flagged by that same rule.
? broken(Arrest).
# => FALSE

# ── BEGINNING, DURING, AND AN EXPLICIT END ───────────────────────────────────
# `happen(x1)` is "x1 commences/initiates/starts/begins to occur" (gismu cfari) — the
# BEGIN relation. `concurrent(x1, x2)` is "x1 is current at/during/simultaneous with x2"
# (gismu cabna). `end(x1, x2)` is "x1 is an end/termination of process x2" (gismu fanmo).
# All arity 1-2, none numeric.
happen(Hearing).
concurrent(Custody, Appeal).
end(Release, Custody).

? happen(Hearing).
# => TRUE

? concurrent(Custody, Appeal).
# => TRUE

? end(Release, Custody).
# => TRUE

# Begun-and-not-ended is the second spelling of "still running", and a rule reads it.
:accept
all $e: happen($e) & ~end(Release, $e) -> occurrence($e).

? occurrence(Hearing).
# => TRUE

# ── A MAGNITUDE MAY BE SYMBOLIC ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The calendar units (`year`, `month`, `week`, `full_day`, `hour`, `minute`, `second`)
# take their magnitude in an ORDINARY x2 place labelled `object` — the engine does not
# require a numeral there, so a Name constant states a term without a digit. What this
# buys is a term that can be COMPARED only by rules the KB writes; no arithmetic follows
# from it, and `Two` here is opaque. Pinned so a digit-banning KB knows the door exists.
year(Term, Two).

? year(Term, Two).
# => TRUE

:expect-pins 23
